= Agent memory in artificial intelligence — Simple =

'''Agent memory''' is information an AI agent keeps so it can use past experience later.

An agent might remember:

* what happened earlier in a task;
* facts learned from a user;
* actions that failed;
* previous results;
* useful procedures.

Agent memory is not the same as a model's context window.

It is also not automatically the same as a vector database or retrieval system.

Those can be parts of a memory system.

